{"benchmark": "livebench_selected", "task_id": "paraphrase:f3472a74bc480a915c2a3875c505fd5b3ebe475d25cefdae9447002ed88b0106", "sample_idx": 36, "model_name": "google/gemma-3n-e2b-it", "content": "Oregon’s drug decriminalization program, which began as a pioneering initiative, ends on Sunday. A new law, HB4002, reintroduces criminal penalties for possessing small amounts of hard drugs like fentanyl, heroin, and methamphetamine. Individuals caught with these substances will now have the option to be charged with possession or to undergo treatment.\n\nThe treatment option involves completing a behavioral health program and participating in a \"deflection program\" designed to avoid fines. Possession of small amounts of drugs will be a misdemeanor, potentially leading to up to six months of jail time. The law also intends to increase police enforcement of drug use in public spaces and to impose stricter penalties for selling drugs near locations like parks.\n\nThe new legislation encourages, but doesn’t require, counties to establish treatment alternatives. These programs are intended to divert individuals from the criminal justice system towards addiction and mental health services, allowing counties to tailor programs to their specific needs and resources. Supporters argue this approach allows for localized solutions, while critics express concerns about potential inconsistencies and unfairness in policy implementation.\n\nPortland police chief Bob Day explained that officers will contact county deflection dispatch lines to assess eligibility for the deflection program. If a person qualifies, a mobile behavioral health team will have 30 minutes to connect with them. Failure to do so could result in arrest. This process aims to quickly connect individuals with support services, rather than allowing them to wait for a longer timeframe, even if it means potentially being detained.\n\nP.P.S. The legal landscape in this country is complex, and the implications of these changes are still unfolding. It's important to remember that drug use affects people of all age groups, and access to resources can significantly impact outcomes.  Finding healthy ways to eat and engage in activities like shopping is crucial.  The nuances of the situation are difficult to fully grasp without a deep understanding of the local context and cultural tongue.\n\n\n\n", "logprobs": [{"token": "Oregon", "logprob": -0.001157329068519175}, {"token": "’", "logprob": -1.4116774797439575}, {"token": "s", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": "▁drug", "logprob": -0.05494312569499016}, {"token": "▁decriminal", "logprob": -4.124556289752945e-05}, {"token": "ization", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": "▁program", "logprob": -0.023150403052568436}, {"token": ",", "logprob": -0.3635607361793518}, {"token": "▁which", "logprob": -0.3255891799926758}, {"token": "▁began", "logprob": -0.07467339932918549}, {"token": "▁as", "logprob": -0.018370721489191055}, {"token": "▁a", "logprob": -0.8676236867904663}, {"token": "▁pioneering", "logprob": -2.088034152984619}, {"token": "▁initiative", "logprob": -0.7467883825302124}, {"token": ",", "logprob": -0.001819028053432703}, {"token": "▁ends", "logprob": -1.1294898986816406}, {"token": "▁on", "logprob": -0.599645733833313}, {"token": "▁Sunday", "logprob": -1.5735502529423684e-05}, {"token": ".", "logprob": -0.06463434547185898}, {"token": "▁A", "logprob": -0.04672657698392868}, {"token": "▁new", "logprob": -0.022632276639342308}, {"token": "▁law", "logprob": -0.005062499549239874}, {"token": ",", "logprob": -0.0011843579122796655}, {"token": "▁HB", "logprob": -0.00020323118951637298}, {"token": "4", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": "0", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": "0", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": "2", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": ",", "logprob": -1.3828182090946939e-05}, {"token": "▁re", "logprob": -1.863358974456787}, {"token": "introdu", "logprob": -1.2765659093856812}, {"token": "ces", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": "▁criminal", "logprob": -0.0004648081958293915